\section{The servers}
\label{sec:servers}

Three questions are enough, because what is at stake is the store and the log and
not the kinds of question.  The builds below ask the same three again, so a build
really merges over the entries the server is reading.

<<constants>>=
SET_UP_QUESTIONS = """
import json
from mentipy.questions import OpenQuestion, MCQuestion
from mentipy.store import Store
store = Store("mentipy.json", min_prefix=4)
print(json.dumps({
    "first": store.register(OpenQuestion("Open one?")),
    "second": store.register(OpenQuestion("Open two?")),
    "choice": store.register(MCQuestion("Pick?", ("A", "B"))),
}))
"""
OPEN_QUESTIONS = ("first", "second")
QUESTIONS = (*OPEN_QUESTIONS, "choice")
