\section{The readers}
\label{sec:readers}

An answer that reached the log but no longer reaches a lecturer is as lost as one
that never arrived, so each of the ways to read answers gets asked.  The answer log
is read as raw lines here, without Mentipy's reader, since that reader is under test:
any line that does not parse is counted and reported.  The last line must be empty,
as the file ends in a newline unless a write was cut off.

<<run methods>>=
def _read_answer_log(self):
    values, malformed = {}, 0
    lines = self.answer_log.read_bytes().split(b"\n") if (
        self.answer_log.exists()
    ) else [b""]
    for line in lines[:-1]:
        if not line.strip():
            continue
        try:
            entry = json.loads(line)
            values.setdefault(entry["hash"], []).append(entry["value"])
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
            malformed += 1
    return values, malformed, len(lines[-1])
@

For a question, four readers give the answers themselves, the raw log, [[results.json]]
and both formats of [[mentipy export]], and two give only a count, the results page and
[[mentipy view]].  A reader that fails is treated as one that found nothing rather than
as a crash of this program: that is what it would mean to a lecturer, and it keeps the
numbers of the other readers in the report.

