\section{Running it}

From the root of the repository:

\begin{description}
\item[Everything] [[make stress]] tangles the source and this program and runs all the
  scenarios, 25 seconds each, for about five minutes in all with the readers.
\item[A choice] [[make stress STRESSFLAGS="builds kill-server --seconds 10"]].
\item[Looking closer] [[--keep]] leaves the store, the log and [[server.log]] of each
  scenario in the working directory, and says where.
\item[Another Mentipy] [[--source]] tests the package in another directory.  This is
  how to see the program fail: copy [[src]] somewhere, drop the [[os.write]] from
  [[_append_answer]] for some answers, and run with [[--source]] there.
\end{description}

It can catch a real race and not only a deliberate gap.  In a copy where each answer
rewrote the whole log instead of appending to it, with nothing dropped on purpose, it
found 15 of 375 accepted answers lost under [[builds]] and 159 of 1059 under [[burst]],
in eight seconds each.  The program needs POSIX signals and file size limits, and
has only been run on Linux.

